---
description: Prefer graphify knowledge graph for architecture / cross-file questions when graphify-out/ exists
alwaysApply: false
---

When `graphify-out/graph.json` exists and the question is about architecture, file relationships, or “how does X connect to Y”:

- Prefer `graphify query "<question>"`, `graphify path "<A>" "<B>"`, or `graphify explain "<concept>"` before broad Grep/Glob sweeps
- Read `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` for high-level orientation
- After substantial code changes, run `graphify update .` (AST-only) to refresh the graph

If `graphify-out/graph.json` does not exist yet, do not block on graphify — explore normally, or build with `/graphify .` when the user asks.

CLI note (Windows): if `graphify` is not on PATH, use the user Scripts install, e.g. `%APPDATA%\Python\Python313\Scripts\graphify.exe`.
